    "result": "The implementation is complete and verified. Summary of the fix in `packages/frai-gate/src/gate/validate.ts`:\n\n- Added a field parser (`parseFields`/`matchFieldLine`) that recognizes both `- **Label**: value` and `- **Label:** value` styles, and treats indented lines below a field (nested bullets, tables, paragraphs, with blank lines in between) as part of that field's answer rather than \"unanswered.\"\n- `extractTier` and a new `extractSignoff` now pull from the isolated **Tier**/**Sign-off** field text (inline + nested) instead of searching the whole subsection body, so mentions of other tier names in the justification no longer create ambiguity.\n- Added a `NEEDS_HUMAN_INPUT` scan per gate subsection that blocks the check if any `NEEDS HUMAN INPUT` marker remains unresolved.\n\nVerified:\n- All 11 existing tests pass unchanged; no test file edits.\n- `assets/rai-spec-template.md` now produces byte-for-byte the same findings as before the change.\n- `examples/frai-spec-example.md` and `examples/support-triage-demo/FRAI-SPEC.md` still PASS.\n- `examples/support-triage-demo/rai-gate-draft.reference.md` now correctly extracts tier `limited` and reports BLOCK only for its genuinely unresolved `NEEDS HUMAN INPUT` items \u2014 the formatting-noise findings (bad tier match, false \"unanswered field\" on the table/nested answers) are gone.\n- `tsc --noEmit` compiles cleanly; JSON output shape and exit codes unchanged.",
